{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating sensor outcomes from motion commands. The specification encodes safe, conservative exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are chosen deterministically based on obstacle location. Full_rotate is reserved for deadlock recovery. All obstacle events force a turn before resuming exploration, and no state enables both turn directions or forward/turn simultaneously. The design avoids oscillations and ensures steady, safe coverage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception (sensor events) and motion (actuator commands)",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe exploration, deterministic recovery, and alternation between random_walk and move_forward"
  ],
